for row,s in zip(t['slides'],story):
 sec=int(row['start']);chapters.append(f'<li><button data-start="{row["start"]}" onclick="const v=document.querySelector(\'video\');v.currentTime=Number(this.dataset.start);v.play()">{sec//60}:{sec%60:02} · {html.escape(s["title"])}</button></li>')
page=(V/'index.html').read_text(encoding='utf-8').replace('poster="highlight-preview.jpg"','poster="cover.png"')
extra='<section><h2>Lesson chapters</h2><ol style="columns:2;line-height:2">'+''.join(chapters)+f'</ol><p>{len(e["shots"])} pages were captured live with Playwright (GitHub repository, Claude docs and Console sign-in, and the platform running from a fresh clone). Terminal slides reproduce real PowerShell transcripts recorded in C:\\Students; long progress output is condensed. Console and VS Code images are instructor screenshots with the API key hidden. Resource IDs are partly hidden.</p><p><a href="walkthrough-evidence.json">Capture evidence</a> · <a href="narration-script.txt">Narration script</a> · <a href="geometry-audit.json">Highlight geometry</a></p></section><style>button{{background:none;border:0;color:#f2b48f;font:inherit;text-align:left;cursor:pointer}}li{{break-inside:avoid}}@media(max-width:750px){{ol{{columns:1!important}}}}</style>'
if 'Lesson chapters' not in page:page=page.replace('</main>',extra+'</main>')
(V/'index.html').write_text(page,encoding='utf-8');sec=int(r['durationSeconds']);stamp=f'{sec//60}:{sec%60:02}'
catalog=R/'videos/index.html';body=catalog.read_text(encoding='utf-8');card=f'<article data-project="{N}"><span>CLAUDE MANAGED AGENTS · INSTALL AND RUN</span><a href="{N}/index.html"><img loading="lazy" src="{N}/cover.png" alt="{html.escape(TITLE)}"></a><div><h2>{html.escape(TITLE)}</h2><p>Verified · {stamp} · 1080p · Yash narration · {len(e["shots"])} real setup steps</p><a href="{N}/{r["file"]}">MP4</a> · <a href="{N}/index.html">Player and chapters</a></div></article>'
if f'data-project="{N}"' not in body:catalog.write_text(body.replace('<main>','<main>'+card,1),encoding='utf-8')
(V/'README.txt').write_text(f'CLAUDE MANAGED AGENTS: {TITLE.upper()}\nDuration: {stamp}. 1920x1080, 30 fps, H.264/AAC. Inworld Yash, TTS 2, enhanced, balanced delivery, speaking rate 1.25, 48kHz.\n\n33 scenes: cover; roadmap; prerequisites; GitHub repository; Code menu; git clone; ZIP download; README; npm ci; create .env; .env.example; managed:ready; quickstart prerequisites; API key search; API key docs; Console sign-in; Console key list; federation prompt; create key; copy key; paste key in .env; readiness; managed:provision; paste IDs; managed:verify; npm run dev; Home; backend check; offline Lab 01; two PowerShell windows; enabling live mode; useful commands; checklist.\n\nGitHub, Claude docs, Console sign-in and app views were captured live with Playwright. Real run on a fresh clone: git clone, ZIP download, npm ci, .env creation, managed:ready, managed:provision (one agent and one environment created), managed:verify (read-only), npm run dev and separate dev:server/dev:web. No live session was started. The API key shown in the instructor screenshots is hidden and should be revoked after recording.\n\nRebuild (run the terminal steps in C:\\Students first; app capture needs npm run dev there): node scripts/capture-install-run-walkthrough.mjs web; node scripts/capture-install-run-walkthrough.mjs app; python scripts/create-install-run-walkthrough.py; node scripts/capture-install-run-walkthrough-slides.mjs; python scripts/create-install-run-walkthrough.py; python scripts/audit-install-run-walkthrough.py; python -u scripts/build-narrated-presentation.py --project {N}; python scripts/finish-install-run-walkthrough.py\n',encoding='utf-8')
